==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|tick|er}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tɪkə(ɹ)/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪkə(r)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A measuring or reporting device, particularly one which makes a [[tick]]ing sound as the measured events occur.
#: ''The '''ticker''' was showing an increased rate of flow.''
# A [[ticker tape]], either the traditional paper kind or a scrolling message on a screen.
#: ''I checked the prices on the '''ticker''' one last time before placing the trade.''
#: ''To my surprise, the '''ticker''' showed that the deal had already gone through.''
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} The heart.
#: ''My '''ticker''' gave out and I had to go to the hospital for surgery.''
# {{lb|en|birdwatching|slang}} A [[birdwatcher]] who aims to see (and tick off on a list) as many bird species as possible.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|news ticker}}, {{l|en|stock ticker}}

